 16	In this section, we define a Fortress core calculus with overloading
 17	for dotted methods and first-order functions.
 18	We call this calculus \emph{\overloadingcore}.
 19	\overloadingcore\ is an extension of \basiccore\ with overloading.
 20	\revision{revival-calculi}{This calculus predates instantiation exclusion
 21	(\secref{trait-types}, \secref{trait-decls}).
 22	Its only condition on multiple inheritance is its rule
 23	\ruleLabel{ValidMeth}, which constrains pairs of visible methods of one
 24	name, so, as in \basiccore, an object that extends two different
 25	instantiations of a parameterized trait declaring no method is well typed,
 26	and its subtyping rule \sBothRule\ makes the object a subtype of both
 27	instantiations; under the rule it is not a valid Fortress program.
 28	The calculus, its rules and its soundness claim are as the team wrote and
 29	proved them, and are not changed.}
